<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Tonk State</h1><p class="st-meta">1817 CE – 1948 CE · capital Tonk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The only Muslim-ruled state of Rajputana, created in 1817 for the Pathan freebooter Amir Khan in exchange for disbanding his army.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir-khan-of-tonk">Amir Khan</a>, a Pathan soldier of fortune, led a large army in alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashwant-rao-holkar">Yashwant Rao Holkar</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/indore-state">Indore State</a> and plundered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a> for two decades. In 1817 he agreed to disband his troops, and the British confirmed him as Nawab of Tonk with lands granted earlier by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holkars">Holkar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tonk was a 17-gun salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana-agency">Rajputana Agency</a> made up of scattered districts. Nawab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-khan-of-tonk">Muhammad Ali Khan</a> was deposed in 1867 after men acting for him killed members of the family of the Thakur of Lawa. The Nawabs collected Arabic and Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, now kept in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maulana-abul-kalam-azad-arabic-persian-research-institute">Maulana Abul Kalam Azad Arabic Persian Research Institute</a> at Tonk.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tonk acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and in 1948 was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan</a>; it is now a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tonk-state.jpg" alt="Tonk State" width="320" height="203"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tonk.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1817 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tonk</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Amir Khan, Muhammad Ali Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Sunni Islam (ruling house)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dhundhari, Urdu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tonk</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=tonk-state" aria-label="Tonk State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6681 1216 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tonk State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7001 1472L7364 1601M7001 1472L7364 1602M7001 1472L6996 1446"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6996 1446h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7001 1472h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7001 1472h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tonk. <a href="/atlas?year=1882&amp;focus=tonk-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
